<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Robinhood Creek Loop (from Pocket Creek Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:201-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.329021" lon="-121.586759"><ele>1162.9</ele><name>Pocket Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:pocket-creek-sno-park (OSM node 6287637025); confidence: high; pdf_page: 202; book_elev_ft: 3800</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.331250" lon="-121.585300"><ele>1151.4</ele><name>Highway 35 bridge over Newton Creek</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_200-2: OSM Newton Creek under OR 35; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 202; quote: walk 150 yards north down Highway 35, crossing a bridge, to the trail signs west of the highway</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.332000" lon="-121.589500"><ele>1162.7</ele><name>Newton Creek Trail, skid roads</name><desc>source: north-west of the trail signs, as map 42 draws trail 7 running north-west from sno-park E; unmapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 202; quote: Follow the trail as it winds gently uphill along the creek then on old skid roads through scenic forest</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.331560" lon="-121.594360"><ele>1181.8</ele><name>Wide road (NF 3500-670)</name><desc>source: OSM NF 3500-670 node 33446399, 0.6 mi from the sno-park by the trail; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 203; quote: ski 0.6 mile to a wide road where you turn right and ski north 0.4 mile</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.335250" lon="-121.588500"><ele>1144.2</ele><name>Leave the road for the narrow ski trail</name><desc>source: OSM NF 3500-670 node 33430969 at the road's northern bend, 0.39 mi along it; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 203; quote: Turn left, leave the road for a narrow ski trail, and pass through scrubby growth and old clearcuts</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.338000" lon="-121.590700"><ele>1140.7</ele><name>Foot of Bluegrass Ridge 2</name><desc>source: DEM foot of the slope; confidence: low; pdf_page: 203</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.340000" lon="-121.589700"><ele>1126.4</ele><name>Foot of Bluegrass Ridge 3 (old growth, top of the hill)</name><desc>source: DEM foot of the slope; confidence: low; pdf_page: 203; quote: then enter old growth, descend the moderate hill</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.341800" lon="-121.587500"><ele>1109.2</ele><name>Wide road at the foot of the hill (west end of 3520-650)</name><desc>source: west end of USFS road 3520650; map 42 3550 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 203; book_elev_ft: 3550; quote: and reach a wide road. Turn right for the next leg of the loop. The wide road also goes left and climbs along the side of Bluegrass Ridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.337830" lon="-121.577270"><ele>1108.4</ele><name>Turn right off Road 3520 near the highway</name><desc>source: USFS Road 3520 vertex 320 m before OR 35 (0.6 mi from the hill; book 0.9), so the return trail stays west of the highway as map 42 draws it; confidence: low; pdf_page: 203; quote: follow the wide road eastward for 0.9 mile, reenter forest by turning right onto a primitive road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.334800" lon="-121.579600"><ele>1123.6</ele><name>Return trail 1</name><desc>source: about 120 m north-west of OR 35, as map 42 draws the loop's east leg beside the highway; unmapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 203; quote: then follow a trail through open forest to close the loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.333200" lon="-121.583800"><ele>1140.7</ele><name>Return trail 2</name><desc>source: about 120 m north-west of OR 35; unmapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 203</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.331250" lon="-121.585300"><ele>1151.4</ele><name>Newton Creek trailhead (loop closes)</name><desc>source: as the bridge waypoint; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 203</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.329021" lon="-121.586759"><ele>1162.9</ele><name>Pocket Creek Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Robinhood Creek Loop (from Pocket Creek Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Pocket Creek Sno-Park -&gt; Highway 35 bridge over Newton Creek: straight (high), 0.17 mi | 2. Highway 35 bridge over Newton Creek -&gt; Newton Creek Trail, skid roads: straight (low), 0.21 mi | 3. Newton Creek Trail, skid roads -&gt; Wide road (NF 3500-670): straight (low), 0.24 mi | 4. Wide road (NF 3500-670) -&gt; Leave the road for the narrow ski trail: osm (medium), 0.39 mi | 5. Leave the road for the narrow ski trail -&gt; Foot of Bluegrass Ridge 2: straight (low), 0.22 mi | 6. Foot of Bluegrass Ridge 2 -&gt; Foot of Bluegrass Ridge 3 (old growth, top of the hill): straight (low), 0.15 mi | 7. Foot of Bluegrass Ridge 3 (old growth, top of the hill) -&gt; Wide road at the foot of the hill (west end of 3520-650): straight (low), 0.16 mi | 8. Wide road at the foot of the hill (west end of 3520-650) -&gt; Turn right off Road 3520 near the highway: usfs-road (medium), 0.65 mi | 9. Turn right off Road 3520 near the highway -&gt; Return trail 1: straight (low), 0.24 mi | 10. Return trail 1 -&gt; Return trail 2: straight (low), 0.23 mi | 11. Return trail 2 -&gt; Newton Creek trailhead (loop closes): straight (low), 0.15 mi | 12. Newton Creek trailhead (loop closes) -&gt; Pocket Creek Sno-Park (finish): straight (high), 0.17 mi</desc>
